Connect issue order with release, expiry and actual chemical state (@cs-expiry: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @chemical-supply-systems, #source "../sources/Good-Storage-and-Distribution-WHO.lingua#r_64EPQ96J7NE7QCWQ28SPXJ8V4D", #source "../sources/Inventory-Analytics-Rossi.lingua#r_61Y17EAC05XZSS1B28NX17SV7C", #source "../sources/Warehouse-and-Distribution-Science.lingua#r_1QVYHWFDZJB0PMG6V9CB2M4H10", #chemical-supply-systems "../../../inquiry/reproducible-computation/numerics/A-numerical-validation-study.lingua#r_7EY9S6DXHFHSJAGA30W35A4ZD8") { r_51EG5VC98CFTY7FR8ZBTR113N8
**Read:** [Good storage and distribution practices for medical products — WHO](../sources/Good-Storage-and-Distribution-WHO.lingua#r_64EPQ96J7NE7QCWQ28SPXJ8V4D), complete stock-rotation, storage-condition and returned/nonconforming discussions; [Inventory Analytics — Roberto Rossi](../sources/Inventory-Analytics-Rossi.lingua#r_61Y17EAC05XZSS1B28NX17SV7C), complete inventory-system and time-dependent control material; [Warehouse & Distribution Science — Bartholdi and Hackman](../sources/Warehouse-and-Distribution-Science.lingua#r_1QVYHWFDZJB0PMG6V9CB2M4H10), the complete operations and inventory information account.

First-in-first-out follows arrival order; first-expiry-first-out follows the next relevant validity boundary. They agree only under particular histories. A later-arriving material can have an earlier expiry, and a present lot may still be quarantined. Define the status and date conventions before evaluating a policy.

Use an explicit rule that a lot with expiry day e is unavailable for an issue at the beginning of day e. Decide when scheduled release occurs, when demand is served and when expiry is recognised. These are model conventions; actual chemical validity follows the qualified material/state history. A date in a database cannot establish that the storage envelope was maintained.

Draw two lots across four daily periods. Compare issuing by receipt order, expiry order and an inappropriate “largest lot first” rule. Close physical quantity, fulfilled/unfulfilled demand, expired material and remaining quarantined stock. Identify when allocation restrictions, product differences or time-dependent use make a simple greedy policy insufficient. The original exact example isolates one identical-item problem so its mathematical claim can be checked independently; advanced studies add observed chemical quality and real receiving/replenishment constraints.

**Continue:** [Build a numerical validation argument across several kinds of evidence](../../../inquiry/reproducible-computation/numerics/A-numerical-validation-study.lingua#r_7EY9S6DXHFHSJAGA30W35A4ZD8).

